From 475167fa47b367bb7f29e893730a4116247c98fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Kirby <rkirby@nvidia.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 05:52:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] fix(inference): never apply a KV-only prefix skip to a
 hybrid model past its first chunk

`_compute_prefix_match` derives `prefix_skip_tokens` from the KV hash match whenever
the chunk starts block-aligned, and only zeroes it for hybrid models on the first
chunk (`finished == 0`). A hybrid model's Mamba state is restored only on the first
chunk, and only when a Mamba prefix cache exists, so a block-aligned continuation
chunk that hash-matches its blocks skips tokens the recurrent layers never see. The
">= 2 computed tokens" clamp then leaves exactly 256 computed tokens per 16384-token
chunk while attention still reads the matched KV: generation stays mostly coherent
but a few percent of decode steps become confidently wrong.

Memory-only prefix caching (prefix_caching_mamba_gb unset) makes this routine: every
turn re-prefills its whole prompt, chunk boundaries are not Mamba-aligned (that guard
needs the allocator), and a request prefilling alone gets exact 16384-token chunks so
every boundary is aligned. On a 16-node Nemotron-3.5-nano SWE-agent RL smoke this
produced |engine - trainer| logprob spikes >3 nats on 0.5-0.8% of decode tokens past
position 131072 (vs 0.001% with the v2 stack, which defaulted to a 50 GB Mamba cache);
279 of the 334 affected turns reported num_cached_tokens > 0 (median 16128) even though
memory-only mode must report 0, and the engine step log shows solo 256-token prefill
chunks late in every rollout step.

Skip only on the first chunk of a hybrid model with a Mamba-backed restore; every other
chunk recomputes all of its tokens (matched blocks stay deduplicated through the
dummy-block write redirect). Non-hybrid models are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 megatron/core/inference/contexts/dynamic_context.py | 9 ++++-----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/megatron/core/inference/contexts/dynamic_context.py b/megatron/core/inference/contexts/dynamic_context.py
index 13353171c..5bc16a3eb 100644
--- a/megatron/core/inference/contexts/dynamic_context.py
+++ b/megatron/core/inference/contexts/dynamic_context.py
@@ -3223,9 +3223,8 @@ class DynamicInferenceContext(MTPContextMixin, BaseInferenceContext):
         else:
             prefix_skip_tokens = 0
 
-        # Hybrid models with Mamba caching: skip based on Mamba match count.
-        # Only applies to the first chunk (finished == 0); continuation chunks
-        # already had Mamba state restored during the first chunk.
+        # Hybrid models may only skip on the first chunk, backed by a restored
+        # Mamba state; no later boundary has a recurrent state to resume from.
         if self.is_hybrid_model and self.mamba_slot_allocator is not None and finished == 0:
             num_mamba_matched = self._find_mamba_match_count(
                 req=req,
@@ -3249,8 +3248,8 @@ class DynamicInferenceContext(MTPContextMixin, BaseInferenceContext):
                     prefix_skip_tokens = raw_skip
             else:
                 prefix_skip_tokens = 0
-        elif self.is_hybrid_model and finished == 0:
-            if record_mamba_match:
+        elif self.is_hybrid_model:
+            if record_mamba_match and finished == 0:
                 req._mamba_num_matched_blocks = 0
             prefix_skip_tokens = 0
 
